@page "/faq"
@rendermode @(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))

<PageTitle>FAQ — CAE Practice</PageTitle>

<div class="page-shell faq-page">
    <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
    <p class="muted faq-intro">
        Everything about how the trainer works, how your progress is stored, and how to run or extend it.
    </p>

    <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item" open>
            <summary>What is this site?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    A trainer for the <strong>Cambridge C1 Advanced (CAE)</strong> Reading &amp; Use of English
                    paper — all four parts in exam format — plus focused drills for grammar and vocabulary
                    topics (articles, prepositions, phrasal verbs, verb patterns, tenses, conditionals and more).
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do I need an account?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    No. You can practise immediately — your progress is then kept in this browser. If you
                    register, your history is stored on the server and follows you across devices; when you
                    log in for the first time, the work you did anonymously is merged into your account.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How are sets chosen?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    Every task offers 110+ sets of 8 questions (6 for Part 4). A new set is one you have
                    <em>never seen before</em> whenever possible; once you have exhausted the bank, the sets
                    you saw longest ago come back first. Hint usage and revealed answers are excluded from
                    your accuracy statistics.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Are these real Cambridge exam papers?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    No. All content is <strong>original</strong>, written for this site in the CAE format.
                    No Cambridge exam material is reproduced. Exam-style sets follow the real paper's layout;
                    sets labelled <em>drill</em> are sentence-level practice on the same skills.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Why was my answer marked wrong?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    Spelling counts. Case and punctuation are ignored, and common variants are accepted where
                    they exist — after checking, the expected answer (and any accepted alternatives) is shown
                    with an explanation. For Part 4, your answer must include the key word unchanged and stay
                    within three to six words.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How do hints affect my score?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    Hints never reveal the answer — they nudge you towards it. Using them marks the attempt
                    with a 💡 in your history and in your per-task hint rate, but your accuracy is measured
                    the same way. "Show answers" reveals everything and records the attempt as revealed,
                    which is excluded from accuracy statistics entirely.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can I run this myself?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    Yes — it is a standard .NET 8 Blazor app. Locally: <code>dotnet run --project src/PracticingCAE.Web</code>.
                    Anywhere: <code>docker compose up --build</code> — the SQLite database is created and migrated
                    automatically inside the mounted volume, so users and progress survive restarts and upgrades.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How can I add more practice content?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    The content lives as readable JSON. Edit the seed banks in
                    <code>tools/ContentGen/Seeds/</code>, then run <code>dotnet run --project tools/ContentGen</code>.
                    The generator validates every item (answers, hints, explanations, gap counts) and refuses
                    to build if any task would drop below 100 sets.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What happens if my connection drops in the middle of a set?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    Nothing is lost. The site keeps retrying the connection for about two minutes, and a
                    successful reconnect resumes exactly where you were. If the page is reloaded, your current
                    set, answers, hints and result are restored from this browser. Pressing <strong>Next set</strong>
                    or opening the task again from the home page deliberately starts a fresh set.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What happens to my data?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                    Accounts store only an email address and a password hash. Practice attempts are stored to
                    compute your statistics. Nothing is shared with third parties, there are no trackers, and
                    no cookies beyond what login and the anonymous-progress id require.
                </p>
            </div>
        </details>
    </div>
</div>
